<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Article 13 privacy notice draft — restricted preview</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Article 13 privacy notice — evidence-bound draft</h1>
      <p>
        This route is a restricted-preview draft. Bracketed text marks facts
        that must be supplied by the project owner or established by observation
        of the live deployment. It must not be presented as a complete public
        notice until every placeholder is resolved.
      </p>

      <h2>Controller and contact</h2>
      <p data-owner-decision-placeholder="provider-identity">
        [OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: provider/controller identity]
      </p>
      <p data-owner-decision-placeholder="postal-address">
        [OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: complete postal address]
      </p>
      <p data-owner-decision-placeholder="monitored-contact">
        [OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: permanent monitored contact for privacy
        requests]
      </p>

      <h2>Application behavior</h2>
      <p>
        The committed Astro application is a static site. It has no user
        accounts, submission form, product analytics, tracking pixel, external
        embed or client JavaScript. It does not contain application code that
        reads or writes cookies, local storage, session storage, IndexedDB or
        service-worker storage. Following an original-source link is a
        user-initiated navigation to that source, not an embedded request.
      </p>
      <p>
        These statements describe the committed application export. They do not
        establish what the deployment host, CDN or any access-control layer
        processes.
      </p>

      <h2>Live delivery and operational data</h2>
      <p data-deployment-observation-placeholder="request-processing">
        [LIVE DEPLOYMENT OBSERVATION REQUIRED: record request metadata actually
        processed by the host/CDN, the purposes and the applicable legal basis]
      </p>
      <p data-deployment-observation-placeholder="cookies-storage">
        [LIVE DEPLOYMENT OBSERVATION REQUIRED: record any cookies or browser
        storage introduced by the deployed delivery or access-control layer]
      </p>

      <h2>Recipients, subprocessors and transfers</h2>
      <p data-deployment-observation-placeholder="recipients-subprocessors">
        [LIVE ACCOUNT EVIDENCE REQUIRED: identify applicable recipients and
        subprocessors for the services actually enabled]
      </p>
      <p data-deployment-observation-placeholder="transfers-safeguards">
        [LIVE ACCOUNT EVIDENCE REQUIRED: identify any non-EEA transfers and the
        operative safeguard for each transfer]
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p data-deployment-observation-placeholder="retention">
        [LIVE ACCOUNT EVIDENCE REQUIRED: state the retention period or evidenced
        deletion criterion for each operational record]
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to the GDPR's conditions and exceptions, a data subject may
        request access, rectification, erasure or restriction, receive data that
        is portable where that right applies, and object to processing based on
        legitimate interests. A data subject may also complain to a competent
        data-protection supervisory authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        [LIVE/OWNER EVIDENCE REQUIRED: complete any right-to-withdraw wording if
        consent is used, and explain whether providing any personal data is
        required and the consequences of not providing it.]
      </p>

      <h2>Automated decision-making</h2>
      <p>
        The static preview makes no decision about a visitor based on personal
        data and performs no profiling. Operational security measures applied by
        the deployment host must be checked against the live account before this
        statement is finalized.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
